  "question": "A mass on a spring oscillates with period $T$. The spring is cut into two equal halves and the same mass is attached to one half. The new period is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2T$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{T}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{2}\\,T$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{T}{2}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "Each half has twice the force constant: $k' = 2k$. $T \\propto \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{k}}$, so $T' = \\dfrac{T}{\\sqrt{2}}$.",
